# Vaani Backend Architecture

The Vaani backend is built using Go 1.22 with a microservices architecture. Each service is containerized and can be deployed independently.

## Key Services

- **API Gateway** [api-gateway](mdc:backend/services/api-gateway/Dockerfile) - Entry point for client requests, handles routing, authentication, and request validation
- **Media Service** [media-service](mdc:backend/services/media-service/Dockerfile) - Manages audio file storage, processing, and delivery
- **Bulbul Adapter** [bulbul-adapter](mdc:backend/services/bulbul-adapter/Dockerfile) - Integration with Bulbul API for voice transformation
- **Orpheus Inference** [orpheus-inference](mdc:backend/services/orpheus-inference/Dockerfile) - Voice synthesis/recognition using the Orpheus ML model

## Service Communication

Services communicate via gRPC using Protocol Buffers. The API definitions are stored in [shared/proto](mdc:shared/proto/gen.sh) and generated into both Go and Dart code.

## Docker Configuration

All services are containerized using Docker. The Docker Compose file [docker-compose.yml](mdc:backend/infra/docker/docker-compose.yml) allows for local development with all services running together.

## Local Development

For local development, you can use:

```bash
# Start all backend services locally
cd backend && make dev-up

# Run tests
cd backend && make test

# Build Docker images
cd backend && make docker
```

## CI/CD Workflows

Backend CI/CD is handled by GitHub Actions workflows:

- [ci-go.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/ci-go.yml) - Tests and builds backend code on PRs
- [deploy-staging.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml) - Deploys to staging on merge to main
- [release.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/release.yml) - Deploys to production on release tags
